From: Construct <release@constructlinux.org>
Subject: Expect the transform functions' type error where TypeScript 7 reports it

bind_property_full()'s transform functions return what gi-types does not
type, which each call marks with @ts-expect-error on the line before it.
TypeScript 7 reports the mismatched overload on its last argument, null,
instead of on the call: the directive found no error on its line ("Unused
'@ts-expect-error' directive") and the error went unexpected. The
directive moves to the argument it reports on; no code changes.

diff --git a/src/playback-rate-button.ts b/src/playback-rate-button.ts
index afef452..0f8f43d 100644
--- a/src/playback-rate-button.ts
+++ b/src/playback-rate-button.ts
@@ -36,7 +36,6 @@ export class APPlaybackRateButton extends Adw.Bin {
       GObject.BindingFlags.SYNC_CREATE,
     );
 
-    // @ts-expect-error GObject.BindingTransformFunc return arguments are not correctly typed
     window.stream.bind_property_full(
       "rate",
       this._label,
@@ -46,6 +45,7 @@ export class APPlaybackRateButton extends Adw.Bin {
         const rounded = from.toFixed(1);
         return [true, `× ${rounded}`];
       },
+      // @ts-expect-error GObject.BindingTransformFunc return arguments are not correctly typed
       null,
     );
   }
